-- Computer Programming | Mid 1 | easy | 490009351104011 | theory | reused from Computer Programming (440009352104011)
INSERT INTO public."TestsData" ("TestId", "Questions", "Options", "Answers")
VALUES (490009351104011, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Explain Problem solving using flowchart and algorithm in the context of Flowchart & Algorithm. Define it, describe the main principles or steps, and give a relevant example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain History of C in the context of Fundamentals of C. Define it, describe the main principles or steps, and give a relevant example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Decision making statements in the context of Decision statements & looping. Define it, describe the main principles or steps, and give a relevant example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Flowchart- Importance of flowchart in the context of Flowchart & Algorithm. Define it, describe the main principles or steps, and give a relevant example."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning/purpose (2 marks):** An algorithm is a finite sequence of unambiguous steps transforming input to output. It should terminate, be correct and use reasonable time and space.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to syllabus areas such as Flowchart- Importance of flowchart; Symbols of flowchart; how to prepare flowchart; Algorithm design. State relevant components, formulas, assumptions or procedures.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Computer Programming problem; identify the objective, selected method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective and mention a meaningful limitation, error source or trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning/purpose (2 marks):** History of C is covered in “Fundamentals of C”. A good answer should define its purpose, explain its main components or steps, connect it to Structure of C program, compilation and execution, Compiler and Interpreter, C tokens, provide a practical example and state how the result can be checked.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to syllabus areas such as Structure of C program; compilation and execution; Compiler and Interpreter; C tokens. State relevant components, formulas, assumptions or procedures.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Computer Programming problem; identify the objective, selected method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective and mention a meaningful limitation, error source or trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning/purpose (2 marks):** Conditional statements select a path based on a condition. Conditions should cover intended cases and be ordered to avoid unreachable branches.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to syllabus areas such as simple If statement; If-else; nested If- else; else-if ladder. State relevant components, formulas, assumptions or procedures.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Computer Programming problem; identify the objective, selected method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective and mention a meaningful limitation, error source or trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning/purpose (2 marks):** A flowchart represents control flow graphically: oval start/end, rectangle process, parallelogram input/output, diamond decision and arrows.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to syllabus areas such as Problem solving using flowchart and algorithm; Symbols of flowchart; how to prepare flowchart; Algorithm design. State relevant components, formulas, assumptions or procedures.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Computer Programming problem; identify the objective, selected method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective and mention a meaningful limitation, error source or trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

