e stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Combinational Circuits and its implementations appears in “Combinational logic design: 7.5”. Define its role and features, relate it to Arithmetic Circuits - Adders and Subtractor, BCD Adder, Look-Ahead Carry Generator, Multiplier, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Arithmetic Circuits - Adders and Subtractor, BCD Adder, Look-Ahead Carry Generator, Multiplier, Magnitude comparator. Multiplexer and it’s application. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Digital Logic and Design task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

