VALUES (4900932001040135, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic task involving Digital and Analog systems in Digital Logic and Design. Explain the governing principle, justify the method or selection, and include a verification check and limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic task involving Number System: Binary number system (addition in Digital Logic and Design. Explain the governing principle, justify the method or selection, and include a verification check and limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic task involving logic level and pulse waveforms in Digital Logic and Design. Explain the governing principle, justify the method or selection, and include a verification check and limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic task involving elements of digital logic in Digital Logic and Design. Explain the governing principle, justify the method or selection, and include a verification check and limitation."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Digital and Analog systems appears in “Introduction: 1”. Define its role and features, relate it to logic level and pulse waveforms, elements of digital logic, Functions of digital logic, Introduction: 1, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to logic level and pulse waveforms, elements of digital logic, Functions of digital logic, Introduction: 1. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Digital Logic and Design task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Number System: Binary number system (addition appears in “Number systems and binary codes : 6”. Define its role and features, relate it to subtraction, multiplication, Division), Octal and Hexadecimal Number system, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to subtraction, multiplication, Division), Octal and Hexadecimal Number system, Conversion from binary to decimal. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Digital Logic and Design task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** logic level and pulse waveforms appears in “Introduction: 1”. Define its role and features, relate it to Digital and Analog systems, elements of digital logic, Functions of digital logic, Introduction: 1, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Digital and Analog systems, elements of digital logic, Functions of digital logic, Introduction: 1. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Digital Logic and Design task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** elements of digital logic appears in “Introduction: 1”. Define its role and features, relate it to Digital and Analog systems, logic level and pulse waveforms, Functions of digital logic, Introduction: 1, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Digital and Analog systems, logic level and pulse waveforms, Functions of digital logic, Introduction: 1. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Digital Logic and Design task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

